msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:62
#: 51563be0d23a4522bbd75a514270fc73
msgid "Markdown style guide and conventions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:65
#: 7e2cf2a3659946078e5c3264b97c4e93
msgid ""
"*Also see* :doc:`How to edit the website </developer/general/how-to-edit-the-"
"website>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:67
#: 0356d7ea4d0c478b952f9635f4a33aa9
msgid ""
"Some of the Qubes OS website pages are stored as plain text Markdown files "
"in the `qubesos.github.io <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubesos.github.io>`__ "
"repository. When making contributions to Markdown files, please observe the "
"following style conventions. If you’re not familiar with Markdown syntax, "
"`this <https://daringfireball.net/projects/markdown/>`__ is a great resource."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:71
#: 195baa6f163741d5a2fa3bb75e99dd28
msgid "Hyperlink syntax"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:73
#: 3b93f5a11b99467e9fce3dc2f54e113f
msgid ""
"Use non-reference-style links like :code:`[website](https://example.com/)`. "
"Do *not* use reference-style links like ``[website][example]``, ``[website]"
"[]`` or ``[website]``. This facilitates the localization process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:76
#: 4a2ee9fe4d2f4c84af623fb185772f33
msgid "Relative vs. absolute links"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:78
#: 2212c6bddf0f49a7b2905dafed4d562f
msgid ""
"Always use relative rather than absolute paths for internal website links. "
"For example, use ``/donate/`` instead of ``https://www.qubes-os.org/donate/"
"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:80
#: 8aa872d428c5435d8086a2d3c847a079
msgid "You may use absolute URLs in the following cases:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:82
#: 9975ecb8ae87490c957ebc0d112bb13a
msgid "External links"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:83
#: 8747957e2ef54347a8c5b3a63a70f66e
msgid ""
"URLs that appear inside code blocks (e.g., in comments and document "
"templates, and the plain text reproductions of `QSBs <https://www.qubes-os."
"org/security/qsb/>`__ and `Canaries <https://www.qubes-os.org/security/"
"canary/>`__), since they’re not hyperlinks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:84
#: 1df7c81a5aa34b7db82d7c9b5bed1cbe
msgid ""
"Git repo files like ``README.md`` and ``CONTRIBUTING.md``, since they’re not "
"part of the website itself but rather of the auxiliary infrastructure "
"supporting the website"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:87
#: b4aac17888c646d79b38a61188a51012
msgid ""
"This rule is important because using absolute URLs for internal website "
"links breaks:"
msgstr ""

